{
  "company_name": "PartsVault Industrial",
  "industry": "Machinery",
  "use_case": "Spare parts inventory optimization and demand planning",
  "space_title": "PartsVault Industrial - Spare Parts Optimization 📦",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Machinery\n\n**Use case:** Spare Parts Inventory Optimization\n\nPartsVault Industrial — MRO and spare-parts inventory analytics across parts categories and warehouses. Inventory Planners and MRO Buyers manage reorder triggers and stockout risk daily; the VP Supply Chain and CFO use it to optimize working capital tied up in spares, balance carrying cost against service level, and reduce emergency-order premiums.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Inventory turnover ratio — MRO benchmark 2–4x, leaders 6x+\n- Fill rate / service level (%) — target ≥95% for critical spares\n- Stockout events — direct downtime risk\n- Carrying cost ($) — typical 20–30% of inventory value annually\n- Days of supply — target 30–90 days for MRO\n- Emergency orders — premium-cost indicator\n- Inventory value ($) — working-capital tied up in spares\n- Lead time (days) — supplier responsiveness benchmark\n\n**Data sources**\n- `parts_transactions` — issues/receipts/returns/scrap by part with quantity, unit cost, warehouse, urgency\n- `inventory_snapshots` — weekly on-hand, reorder point, on-order, days of supply, stockout risk, value\n- `inventory_kpi_monthly` — monthly turnover, fill rate, stockouts, carrying cost, emergency orders, lead time",
  "schema_basename": "mach_spare_parts",
